Subject: ps2xRuntime: DMA source chains no longer cut at 4,096 tags; every early end logged

The chain walker of DMA channels 0/1/2 (VIF0, VIF1, GIF) stopped after 4,096 tags and dropped the rest without a
word. Rule of Rose's i3r chain has ~14,400 tags per frame (2.9 MB): VU1 never saw the last 70 %, characters
included. Now: safety caps far above any real chain (1M tags, 64 MB) against a looping chain, and the cap, an
untranslatable tag address and a tag outside RAM/scratchpad each print a [DMA] ERROR line (rate-limited after 32).

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_memory.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_memory.cpp
index cf17154..56da90d 100644
